      "question_text": "A study undertaken in West Virginia, USA, shows the relationship between body mass and \nthe probability of having hypertension or type II diabetes. The test subjects in the study were \nclassified as normal, overweight or obese according to their body mass index (BMI).\nProbability \n/ %\n50\n45\n40\n35\n30\n25\n20\n15\n10\n5\n0\nKey:\n type II diabetes\n hypertension\n \nNormal \nOverweight \nObese\n[Source: adapted from E Thoenen, (2002), Obesity: Facts, Figures, Guidelines. \nDepartment of Health and Human Resources, West Virginia Health Statistic Center.]\n \n(a) \nIdentify the increased probability of an obese person having hypertension relative to \nsomeone who has normal weight.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n(b) \nExplain how the administration of a drug that stimulates the leptin receptors in the \nhypothalamus could help treat obesity.\n[3]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n(Option D continues on the following page)\n\n32EP28\n– 28 –\nN16/4/BIOLO/SP3/ENG/TZ0/XX\n(Option D continued)",
